    "note": "GLB member with its Textures/colormap.png (all 32 clips are inside the GLB; no separate animation file). Matched to mini-female-a so the pair reads as one set: height 1.1 m (Kenney minis are chibi, the head is about 40 % of the body, so a real adult scale would make the head huge; 1.1 m keeps the head near real size), noon script with the same role pairs, faceted shading. The GLB rest pose is a T-pose, so views use idle@0. Ground: moving clips use ground clamp; sit, drive and the wheelchair poses are lifted onto the ground plane (set their lift to 0 to seat him on a chair or wheelchair at the authored height). The arm stubs of this character stay above the soles, so no clip needs sinkAllowed. The sprint and die clips are authored with real air time (bounding steps, a hop back before landing)."
